  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">AMECEA Conflict Management and Response Capacity Strengthening</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will be carried out in the AMECEA Region.  Within the countries, there will be a focus to work with the national conferences that have experienced conflict related to electioneering processes and governance.The project proposes to build the capacities of AMECEA collaborators to directly work with communities, governments and the private sector.
The proposed project will be achieved through strengthening the skills of the conferences as well as the various conflict management and response actors within the region through training and sensitization.  It will involve continued facilitation of conferences (Focal Persons) to play an important role in the operationalization of expected conflict management forums and AMECEA&#x2019;s effectiveness. Community civic dialogue and formulation of community peace agreements, strengthening of the national Conflict Early Warning and Early Response mechanisms through the Conferences in Djibouti, Eritrea, Ethiopia, Kenya, Uganda and Tanzania are core components of the project.</narrative>
  </description>
